### Bull Board — http://localhost:4000/admin/queues
# Open in browser to inspect the process-order queue, retry failed jobs, etc.

### Create an order — triggers outbox → queue → idempotent worker flow
POST http://localhost:4000/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "usr_123",
  "total": 49.99,
  "items": [
    { "productId": "prod_1", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### Create another order
POST http://localhost:4000/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "usr_456",
  "total": 129.99,
  "items": [
    { "productId": "prod_2", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productId": "prod_3", "quantity": 3 }
  ]
}

### Test Idempotency-Key — first request (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: idem-001

{
  "customerId": "usr_idem",
  "total": 79.99,
  "items": [{ "productId": "prod_y", "quantity": 1 }]
}

### Test Idempotency-Key — retry with same key + body (expect 201 cached)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: idem-001

{
  "customerId": "usr_idem",
  "total": 79.99,
  "items": [{ "productId": "prod_y", "quantity": 1 }]
}

### Test Idempotency-Key — same key, different body (expect 409 Conflict)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: idem-001

{
  "customerId": "usr_different",
  "total": 99.99,
  "items": [{ "productId": "prod_z", "quantity": 2 }]
}

### Test Retry — triggers 3 BullMQ attempts with exponential backoff (2s, 4s, 8s)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/orders?fail=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "usr_retry",
  "total": 99.99,
  "items": [{ "productId": "prod_x", "quantity": 1 }]
}
